  - Mathlib
abstract: >-
  A complete, sorry-free Lean 4 formalization of the paper "Factorial
  Monoids and (N,x): An Axiomatic Characterization" (E. Zambrano,
  under review at Semigroup Forum): a reduced commutative monoid is
  factorial if and only if it satisfies (WFD), (TD), and (CFI), and
  the four axioms {WFD, TD, CFI, CCA} hold if and only if the monoid
  is isomorphic to the multiplicative positive integers. Includes all
  five independence counterexamples and an interactive dependency map
  of the proof.
